WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
08:15 — Morning ticks. While toast browns, Priya opens the medicine tracker on her iPhone and ticks Dad’s morning pills in the order the clinic printed — large enough to read without glasses.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:13.000
11:00 — Clinic preview. In the waiting room she flips to the iPad so the nurse can see the full day schedule without flipping through a paper pad full of crossed-out times.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.500
14:30 — Notes after the visit. Back home she journals what the doctor said on her laptop — dose change, next bloodwork date — while it is still fresh, still private on the device.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:26.000
19:00 — Evening meds. Evening ticks happen on the phone again; she stands at the counter and clears each row before dinner, no scavenger hunt through blister packs.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.500
21:30 — Tomorrow’s plan. Before her brother visits she leaves Tomorrow open on the laptop so he can glance the plan without asking Dad to “remember everything.”

